  partName: Blade13
  description: The Blade13 is a tiny, elongated blade positioned at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, fabricated from Blades texture material, functioning to direct
    and accelerate the airflow through the engine, with a notable detail being its
    unique texture that enhances its aerodynamic properties and reduces energy losses.
    Its elongated shape provides a larger surface area, enabling more efficient energy
    transfer, and its position in the compressor stage makes it vital for the engine's
    ability to generate thrust. By optimizing airflow and minimizing turbulence,
    Blade13 plays a crucial role in the engine's overall efficiency and performance.
